# Hidden Volcano: "This land enters tapped", "{T}: Add {R}" and "{4}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice this land: Discover 4. Activate only as a
# sorcery." It enters tapped and untaps with the next turn; it taps for {R} alone (Undo takes it back). The discover is refused with only
# four other sources ({4}{R} needs five besides the land itself), with a spell on the stack, and outside a main phase (all with the five
# sources otherwise available); then on a later turn it exiles from the top of the library past a Mountain (a land) and Fire Elemental (mana
# value 5, one more than discover 4) and casts Hill Giant (mana value 4, exactly the limit) for free. The land is sacrificed as a
# cost, so it is in the graveyard when the discover happens, and the two cards skipped go to the bottom of the library
# (CR 701.57a, 602.5d, 118.12).

